# Citation metadata for this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" button from this file, and Zenodo
# uses it to fill in the archived record. Validate after every edit:
#   pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate
#
# TODO before the first release (see RELEASING.md):
#   - add ORCID iDs:            orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
#   - add the other authors (form below), with affiliations and ORCIDs
#   - add `license: <SPDX id>` once LSU and the sponsor confirm the license
#   - set `date-released` and, after Zenodo mints it, `doi` (concept DOI)
#   - update `repository-code` after the transfer to the organization account
#
#   - family-names: <Family name>
#     given-names: <Given names>
#     affiliation: Louisiana State University
#     orcid: "https://orcid.org/<ORCID>"
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "COE-CHIRP: A software-based CHIRP sonar system to track mudline elevation during dredging"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Ikaika
    affiliation: Louisiana State University
abstract: >-
  COE-CHIRP turns a commercial CHIRP sonar into a remotely controlled,
  cloud-connected instrument for tracking mudline elevation in real time
  during marsh-creation dredging. It contains a Flutter mobile app and a
  React web app for triggering scans and analysing bathymetry and
  Instrumented Settlement Plate (ISP) data, the AWS Lambda backend, the
  on-site controller that drives the sonar's companion app on a rooted
  Android phone, a Jupyter notebook for settling-column validation tests,
  and STL files for the 3D-printed sonar mount.
repository-code: "https://github.com/iittqq/COE-CHIRP"
keywords:
  - CHIRP sonar
  - mudline
  - dredging
  - marsh creation
  - settlement plate
  - bathymetry
  - coastal restoration
  - Louisiana
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: "Developing a Software-based CHIRP Sonar System to Track Mudline Elevation During Dredging"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: Ikaika
    thesis-type: "Master's thesis"
    department: Department of Computer Science and Engineering
    institution:
      name: Louisiana State University
    year: 2026
